    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/a50bcc9204cd4ed3223866d13ab80818-ChatGPT Image Oct 16, 2025, 09_07_05 PM.png",
    "long_instructions": "## **Do This**\r\n\r\n**Expected Behavior:**\r\nClicking the **Next** button should show a **new photo and caption** on the page.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n1. **Test it:**\r\n   Run the code and click the button once.\r\n   What happens (or doesn’t happen)?\r\n\r\n2. **Check the basics:** Look for small mistakes that can break the connection between the button and the action.\r\n\r\n::: details [View Debugging Checklist]\r\n- **Selector match:** Does the JavaScript selector match the HTML `id` or `class` exactly?\r\n- **Element exists:** Is that element actually on the page?\r\n- **Order:** Are elements selected before they’re used?\r\n- **Event setup:** Is `'click'` spelled right (not `'onclick'`)?\r\n- **Handler:** Does the code actually change the page (text, image, etc.)?\r\n:::\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n3. **Ask AI for help:** If you're stuck, describe what's happening and ask:\r\n\r\n   > Why isn't this button working? Here's the error or result: [insert error here]. Explain it in beginner terms and suggest what to check first.\r\n\r\n4. **Fix and verify:** Work with AI to make one precise change. If it's still not working, discuss what to try next and keep refining until the feature behaves as expected.",
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <title>Photo Carousel</title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"topbar\">\n      <div id=\"avatar\"></div>\n      <h3 id=\"brand\">PhotoFeed</h3>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"post\">\n      <img id=\"photo1\" src=\"photo1.png\" alt=\"A scenic coastline at sunset\" width=\"300\">\n      <img id=\"photo2\" src=\"photo2.png\" alt=\"A pine forest trail with tall trees\" width=\"300\">\n\n      <div id=\"actions\">\n        <button id=\"next\">Next</button>\n      </div>\n\n      <p id=\"caption\">Sunset on the coast</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": " body {\n  font-family: sans-serif;\n  background-color: #fafafa;\n  text-align: center;\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\n#topbar {\n  background-color: white;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\n  padding: 10px;\n}\n\n#avatar {\n  display: inline-block;\n  width: 28px;\n  height: 28px;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7a59, #ffd15c);\n  vertical-align: middle;\n}\n\n#brand {\n  display: inline-block;\n  margin: 0 0 0 8px;\n  vertical-align: middle;\n}\n\n#post {\n  background-color: white;\n  border: 1px solid #ddd;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  width: 320px;\n  margin: 20px auto;\n  padding-bottom: 10px;\n}\n\n#photo1,\n#photo2 {\n  width: 100%;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\n}\n\n#photo2 {\n  display: none;\n}\n\n#actions {\n  margin: 10px;\n}\n\n#next {\n  border: 1px solid #ddd;\n  background-color: white;\n  padding: 6px 12px;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n#caption {\n  margin: 10px;\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "// When the button is clicked, hide the first photo and show the second one\ndocument.querySelector(\"#next\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  document.querySelector(\"#caption\").textContent = \"Morning trail through the pines\";\n  document.querySelector(\"#photo1\").style.display = \"none\";\n  document.querySelector(\"#nextPhoto\").style.display = \"block\";\n});\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        },
